{"extensions":{"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:islam:tafsir-sample-baseline","descriptor":{"availability":"bundled","byte_size":20480,"locations":["https://archive.org/details/classical-quran-tafsir-sample"],"media_type":"application/json","retrieved_at":"2026-08-28T00:00:00Z","sha256":"pinned-quran-tafsir-sample-baseline-v1"},"institution":"mw:institution:quranic-studies-archive","language":"ar","provenance":"mw:provenance:islam:tafsir-sample","rights":{"attribution":"Classical public domain Quran commentary and exegesis extracts.","license_expression":"CC0-1.0","redistribution":"permitted","status":"public_domain"}}},"id":"mw:artifact:islam:tafsir-sample-baseline","kind":"source.snapshot","labels":[{"language":"en","role":"preferred","value":"Classical Quran Commentary (Tafsir) Sample artifact"}],"record_type":"resource"}
{"extensions":{"textual":{"delimiter":":","units":["surah","ayah"],"work":"mw:work:islam:tafsir-sample"}},"id":"mw:citation-scheme:islam:tafsir-sample:surah-ayah","kind":"textual.citation_scheme","labels":[{"language":"en","role":"preferred","value":"Tafsir commentary surah-ayah citation scheme"}],"record_type":"resource"}
{"extensions":{"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:islam:tafsir-sample-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:islam:tafsir-sample"},"textual":{"genre":"commentary_text","language":"ar","representation":"source","script":"Arab","target":"mw:passage:islam:tafsir:1:1","text":"افتتح به كتاب الله تعالى تبركا وتيمنا، والباء للاستعانة أو للمصاحبة، واسم الله تعالى أعظم الأسماء."}},"id":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:1:1:ar","kind":"textual.content","record_type":"resource"}
{"extensions":{"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:islam:tafsir-sample-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:islam:tafsir-sample"},"textual":{"derived_from":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:1:1:ar","language":"en","representation":"translation","script":"Latn","target":"mw:passage:islam:tafsir:1:1","text":"The Book of Allah is begun with this formula for blessing and seeking aid; the preposition bi indicates seeking assistance, and Allah is the greatest of names."}},"id":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:1:1:en","kind":"textual.content","record_type":"resource"}
{"extensions":{"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:islam:tafsir-sample-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:islam:tafsir-sample"},"textual":{"derived_from":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:1:1:ar","language":"id","representation":"translation","script":"Latn","target":"mw:passage:islam:tafsir:1:1","text":"Kitab Allah Ta’ala dibuka dengan kalimat ini untuk memohon keberkahan dan pertolongan; huruf ba’ bermakna permohonan pertolongan, dan nama Allah adalah nama yang paling agung."}},"id":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:1:1:id","kind":"textual.content","record_type":"resource"}
{"extensions":{"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:islam:tafsir-sample-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:islam:tafsir-sample"},"textual":{"genre":"commentary_text","language":"ar","representation":"source","script":"Arab","target":"mw:passage:islam:tafsir:1:2","text":"الحمد هو الثناء بالجميل على جهة التعظيم، والرب هو المالك والمربي لجميع الخلائق بنعمه."}},"id":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:1:2:ar","kind":"textual.content","record_type":"resource"}
{"extensions":{"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:islam:tafsir-sample-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:islam:tafsir-sample"},"textual":{"derived_from":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:1:2:ar","language":"en","representation":"translation","script":"Latn","target":"mw:passage:islam:tafsir:1:2","text":"Praise (al-hamd) is laudation for beauty and virtue with exaltation, and the Lord (al-Rabb) is the Master and Nurturer of all creation through His blessings."}},"id":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:1:2:en","kind":"textual.content","record_type":"resource"}
{"extensions":{"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:islam:tafsir-sample-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:islam:tafsir-sample"},"textual":{"derived_from":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:1:2:ar","language":"id","representation":"translation","script":"Latn","target":"mw:passage:islam:tafsir:1:2","text":"Al-Hamd adalah pujian dengan segala kebaikan disertai pengagungan, dan ar-Rabb adalah Pemilik serta Pemelihara seluruh makhluk dengan nikmat-nikmat-Nya."}},"id":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:1:2:id","kind":"textual.content","record_type":"resource"}
{"extensions":{"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:islam:tafsir-sample-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:islam:tafsir-sample"},"textual":{"genre":"commentary_text","language":"ar","representation":"source","script":"Arab","target":"mw:passage:islam:tafsir:112:1","text":"قل يا محمد لمن سألك عن صفة ربك: هو الله الأحد، الفرد الذي لا نظير له ولا وزير."}},"id":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:112:1:ar","kind":"textual.content","record_type":"resource"}
{"extensions":{"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:islam:tafsir-sample-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:islam:tafsir-sample"},"textual":{"derived_from":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:112:1:ar","language":"en","representation":"translation","script":"Latn","target":"mw:passage:islam:tafsir:112:1","text":"Say, O Muhammad, to whoever asks about the attribute of your Lord: He is Allah, the One, the Unique who has no equal or partner."}},"id":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:112:1:en","kind":"textual.content","record_type":"resource"}
{"extensions":{"source":{"artifact":"mw:artifact:islam:tafsir-sample-baseline","provenance":"mw:provenance:islam:tafsir-sample"},"textual":{"derived_from":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:112:1:ar","language":"id","representation":"translation","script":"Latn","target":"mw:passage:islam:tafsir:112:1","text":"Katakanlah wahai Muhammad kepada siapa pun yang bertanya tentang sifat Tuhanmu: Dialah Allah Yang Maha Esa, Yang Tunggal tiada tandingan dan sekutu bagi-Nya."}},"id":"mw:content:islam:tafsir:112:1:id","kind":"textual.content","record_type":"resource"}
